{
  "_ulid": "01KJS7PDW5GQQX9WQ2C7C1JNRX",
  "slugs": [],
  "title": "Add --text flag to kspec session log show to replay agent output",
  "type": "task",
  "description": "kspec session log show has no way to read the actual text response from a completed agent invocation. The session.update events contain content blocks with the agent's text, but --events only shows event metadata, not content.\n\nFix: Add a --text flag to session log show that extracts and prints the assistant text from session.update events in chronological order.\n\nImplementation details:\n- Events are stored in .kspec/sessions/<session-id>/events.jsonl\n- Filter for type === 'session.update'\n- From each event's data.content array, collect blocks with type === 'text'\n- Print the text in order to stdout (no extra formatting — just the content)\n- --text and --events are independent flags (both can be used together or separately)\n- Externalized blobs: if content is a blob pointer, resolve it (same logic as --resolve-blobs)\n\nRelevant files:\n- src/cli/commands/session/log.ts — session log show command\n- src/session/ — session event reading utilities\n\nWorkaround (until fixed):\n  cat .kspec/sessions/<id>/events.jsonl | python3 -c \"\n  import sys, json\n  for line in sys.stdin:\n    e = json.loads(line)\n    if e.get('type') == 'session.update':\n      for block in (e.get('data',{}).get('content') or []):\n        if isinstance(block, dict) and block.get('type') == 'text':\n          print(block.get('text',''), end='')\n  \"\n\nTest: Integration test that creates a session with known text output and verifies --text prints it.\n\nSpec ACs to cover: @session-log-show ac-11 (--text flag replays assistant text)",
  "spec_ref": "@session-log-show",
  "meta_ref": null,
  "plan_ref": null,
  "status": "pending",
  "blocked_by": [],
  "depends_on": [],
  "context": [],
